package main

const pageHTML = `<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>S3 Auditor</title><style>body{font:16px system-ui;background:#0c1728;color:#e0ebf7;max-width:1100px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 24px}section{background:#192a40;padding:24px;border-radius:12px;margin:20px 0}input,textarea,select{display:block;background:#0c1728;color:white;padding:10px;border:1px solid #819ab8;border-radius:5px;width:90%;max-width:600px;margin:8px 0}label{display:block;margin:14px 0}button{background:#8ae2bb;color:#102332;border:0;padding:12px;border-radius:6px;font-weight:bold;margin:8px 0;cursor:pointer}a{color:#a3d4ff}td,th{padding:12px;text-align:left;border-bottom:1px solid #52647b;overflow-wrap:anywhere}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}small{color:#b7cadd}.notice{padding:20px;background:#263e56;border-radius:8px}.scroll{overflow-x:auto}summary{cursor:pointer}</style><h1>S3 Auditor</h1><p>Configuration evidence. Focused remediation. Verified reassessment.</p><p class="notice">Read-only AWS tool. Checks bucket policy public status and bucket-level Public Access Block only. Account controls, ACLs, access points and effective anonymous access are outside scope.</p>{{if .Message}}<p role="status" class="notice">{{.Message}}</p>{{end}}<section><h2>Start a scan</h2><form method="post" action="/?token={{.Token}}"><button name="action" value="demo">Run offline synthetic demo</button></form><details><summary>Scan an authorized AWS account</summary><p>Uses your AWS credential chain and signed-in profile. Confirm your profile before submitting. Choose the bucket region; region errors remain unknown. Blank targets discover up to 1000 buckets. May take up to three minutes; other actions wait.</p><form method="post" action="/?token={{.Token}}"><input type="hidden" name="action" value="scan"><label>Profile (blank uses default)<input name="profile"></label><label>Region<input name="region" required placeholder="us-east-1"></label><label>Bucket names (lines or commas; blank discovers)<textarea name="targets"></textarea></label><button>Run read-only assessment</button></form></details></section>{{if .Selected}}<section><h2>Evidence {{if .Selected.Demo}}(SYNTHETIC){{end}}</h2><p>{{.Selected.Scope}} | {{.Selected.At.Format "2006-01-02 15:04:05 UTC"}}</p><a href="/export?token={{.Token}}&id={{.Selected.ID}}">Download JSON evidence</a><div class="scroll"><table><tr><th>Bucket</th><th>Policy observation</th><th>Block observation</th><th>Reassessment</th></tr>{{range .Selected.Reports}}<tr><td>{{.Name}}{{range .Errors}}<p>{{.}}</p>{{end}}</td><td>{{.PolicyState}} (public={{.PublicPolicy}})</td><td>{{.BlockState}} (incomplete={{.IncompleteBlock}})</td><td>{{index $.Delta .Name}}</td></tr>{{end}}</table></div><p>Booleans are not passes when errors exist. A clear reassessment verifies only these two checks.</p>{{range $name,$value:=.Delta}}<small>{{$name}}: {{$value}}</small><br>{{end}}</section>{{if not .Selected.Demo}}<section><h2>Jira handoff</h2><p>Preview: sends selected bucket, account/region, observations, scan time, scope limitations and correlation ID. No object contents, AWS credentials or raw errors. Jira token is used for this request only and never saved. Existing issues receive evidence comments, never automatic closure.</p><form method="post" action="/?token={{.Token}}"><input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{.Selected.ID}}"><label>Bucket<select name="bucket">{{range .Selected.Reports}}<option>{{.Name}}</option>{{end}}</select></label><label>Jira origin<input name="url" required placeholder="https://team.atlassian.net"></label><label>Email<input type="email" name="email" required autocomplete="off"></label><label>API token<input type="password" name="secret" required autocomplete="off"></label><label>Project key<input name="project" placeholder="SEC"></label><label>Issue type<input name="kind" value="Task"></label><button name="action" value="ticket">Create issue / append evidence</button><p>For uncertain creates: search Jira for the correlation shown in delivery records, then link the issue. Do not create another issue blindly.</p><label>Existing Jira key<input name="key" placeholder="SEC-123"></label><button name="action" value="link">Test connection and link issue</button></form></section>{{end}}{{end}}<section><h2>Scan history</h2>{{range .Scans}}<p><a href="/?token={{$.Token}}&scan={{.ID}}">{{.At.Format "2006-01-02 15:04:05"}} | {{.Scope}}</a></p>{{else}}<p>No scans. Try the demo.</p>{{end}}<h3>Jira delivery records</h3>{{range $id,$value:=.Tickets}}<p><small>{{$id}}: {{$value.Key}} ({{$value.State}})</small></p>{{else}}<p>No deliveries.</p>{{end}}</section><footer>Private single-user local tool. Browser closure does not stop the app: press Ctrl+C in the launcher. History is not tamper-proof. Back up the data directory with the app stopped.</footer></html>`
